# Icons

Interface icons are one line set. A filled pictogram does not sit next to a stroke icon for the same kind of control.

## Stroke

- View box `0 0 24 24`.
- `fill: none`, `stroke: currentColor`, `stroke-width: var(--icon-stroke)` (`1.8` in `src/styles.css`).
- `stroke-linecap` and `stroke-linejoin` are `round`.
- Sport marks come only from `SportIcon` in `src/components/sport-icon.tsx`. Every key is a line icon on that same view box.

## One glyph per idea

Reuse the existing path. Do not draw a second pin, heart, chevron, or star.

- Place: `M12 21s7-5.2 7-12a7 7 0 0 0-14 0c0 6.8 7 12 7 12z` plus a circle at `12,9` r `2.4`.
- Direction: `M14 6l-6 6 6 6` and `M10 6l6 6-6 6`.

## Allowed fills

- Rating stars stay filled (`#ffb400`).
- A saved heart may fill; the idle heart stays a stroke.
- Brand marks stay their official shape (Telegram plane). Do not redraw them as generic line icons.

## Do not

- Mix a `0 0 1000 1000` filled library icon with a 24px line icon in one row.
- Set a one-off `stroke-width: 2`, `2.2`, or `2.4` on a custom icon.
- Restyle icons inside `src/components/ui/` (those stay Lucide).
